  "solution": {
    "text": "If the fireman slides down with some acceleration, his apparent weight decreases. For critical condition, rope can bear only <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> of his weight. If <math><mi>a</mi></math> is the minimum acceleration then,<br /><br />Tension in the rope = Breaking stress&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>"
  }
